Mating rituals and the like.

242
00:17:02.563 --> 00:17:07.660
♪ We gather here together ♪

243
00:17:08.319 --> 00:17:10.339
Can't believe I let you talk me into this.

244
00:17:10.363 --> 00:17:11.489
It's research.

245
00:17:11.656 --> 00:17:14.705
You're not allowed to be here.
I could get kicked out of the house.

246
00:17:14.867 --> 00:17:17.336
They're dressed as babies. Ha-ha.

247
00:17:17.495 --> 00:17:20.339
- We're gonna be fine.
- If you're all supposed to be babies...

248
00:17:20.498 --> 00:17:22.184
...then do you also have
to wear the diapers?

249
00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:24.961
- Please don't.
- Should we stay here or go over there?

250
00:17:25.127 --> 00:17:27.004
Please, please stay here. Please.

251
00:17:27.171 --> 00:17:29.674
- Just stay here.
- Okay. We'll stay here. We'll stay.

252
00:17:31.425 --> 00:17:33.848
♪ I for you ♪

253
00:17:34.011 --> 00:17:36.355
♪ And you for me ♪

254
00:17:36.514 --> 00:17:41.236
- ♪ We are here for one another ♪
- Shh.

255
00:17:41.394 --> 00:17:47.072
♪ And together we can fly ♪

256
00:17:47.233 --> 00:17:52.160
♪ We stand by one another ♪

257
00:17:52.321 --> 00:17:57.828
♪ At Alpha Omicron Pi ♪

258
00:17:57.994 --> 00:17:59.792
Welcome, pledges...

259
00:17:59.954 --> 00:18:04.004
- ...to the AO Pi Annual Baby Party.
- Pfft.

260
00:18:04.166 --> 00:18:08.046
Pledges, you will now pair off
with your assigned big sisters.

261
00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:12.016
Pledge Master Olive.

262
00:18:27.732 --> 00:18:28.949
It's okay.

263
00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:30.752
Honestly, I don't get all this.

264
00:18:30.776 --> 00:18:33.529
- It's just for fun.
- Are you back-talking...

265
00:18:33.696 --> 00:18:35.299
- ...Pledge Sara?
- No.

266
00:18:35.323 --> 00:18:37.667
You aren't to speak
unless you are spoken to.

267
00:18:37.825 --> 00:18:41.079
- I realize that. I just...
- Pledge Master Olive...

268
00:18:41.245 --> 00:18:42.997
...discipline your charge.

269
00:19:01.932 --> 00:19:05.402
Pledge Sara, on your knees.

270
00:19:25.956 --> 00:19:27.003
Come on.

271
00:19:49.438 --> 00:19:50.564
Harder.

272
00:19:51.565 --> 00:19:53.533
She's a baby
and needs to be punished.

273
00:20:01.242 --> 00:20:02.744
Twenty.

274
00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:30.377
Stop.

275
00:21:33.292 --> 00:21:34.919
That's enough.

276
00:21:35.669 --> 00:21:38.513
Thank you, Pledge Master Olive.

277
00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:49.354
- I don't wanna talk about it.
- Well, how'd it make you feel?

278
00:21:50.059 --> 00:21:52.619
She doesn't wanna
talk about it, Bill. Why harp on it?

279
00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:56.274
- Because she is blocked. Can't you see?
- Fine.

280
00:21:57.358 --> 00:21:58.985
How did it make you feel?

281
00:21:59.151 --> 00:22:01.870
- I'm the one asking the questions.
- Oh, why should that be?

282
00:22:04.698 --> 00:22:08.043
Go ahead, ask him questions.

283
00:22:08.661 --> 00:22:10.880
How did it make you feel?

284
00:22:12.706 --> 00:22:14.424
How did what make me feel?

285
00:22:17.878 --> 00:22:20.427
Watching me spank that girl.

286
00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.348
Excited...

287
00:22:25.052 --> 00:22:26.725
...repulsed...

288
00:22:27.513 --> 00:22:28.981
...nervous...

289
00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:31.858
- ...aroused.
- Huh.

290
00:22:32.017 --> 00:22:35.362
But my experience
as a spectator is meaningless.

291
00:22:35.521 --> 00:22:39.116
You actually participated. It is
your experience that is worth cataloging.

292
00:22:39.275 --> 00:22:42.199
How did it make you feel?

293
00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:45.072
- Terrible.
- What else?

294
00:22:45.239 --> 00:22:46.491
Ashamed.

295
00:22:48.117 --> 00:22:51.087
- What else?
- Nothing, nothing else.

296
00:22:51.245 --> 00:22:54.715
She won't tell you the truth.
Look at her. She's practically shaking.

297
00:22:54.874 --> 00:22:58.003
Why the hell not? This is the substance
of what we are dealing with.

298
00:22:58.168 --> 00:23:00.887
Because you wanting to know
is perverse, Bill.

299
00:23:01.046 --> 00:23:04.516
If you cannot actually have sex with her,
you'll force her to admit what?

300
00:23:04.675 --> 00:23:07.554
That she experiences desire,
that she was aroused? Oh!

301
00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:08.767
Yes, exactly.

302
00:23:08.929 --> 00:23:11.116
Don't talk about me
as if I were some test subject. I'm here.

303
00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:14.110
Then be here.
You are not still in a convent.

304
00:23:16.729 --> 00:23:19.027
Stop defending her
like she's some wilting violet.

305
00:23:19.189 --> 00:23:23.911
I happen to think there might be value
to keeping one's thoughts to oneself.

306
00:23:29.033 --> 00:23:30.455
Bill...

307
00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:32.583
...when she lies, her...

308
00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:37.174
Her voice shakes.

309
00:23:37.917 --> 00:23:39.134
Wait, come here.

310
00:23:42.713 --> 00:23:44.090
Her hand sweats.

311
00:23:44.256 --> 00:23:46.133
Galvanometer skin tests
were too inconsistent.

312
00:23:46.300 --> 00:23:48.894
Bill, her rhythmic breathing increases.

313
00:23:49.053 --> 00:23:54.230
- Benussi already exhausted that avenue.
- Her heart beats faster.

314
00:23:55.643 --> 00:23:58.863
- Her systolic blood pressure would rise.
- Her systolic blood pressure.

315
00:23:59.021 --> 00:24:01.991
- You could measure that.
- Oh, you could fucking measure that.

316
00:24:02.149 --> 00:24:05.198
- You could measure that. Oh, my God.
- Ha-ha-ha.

317
00:24:06.403 --> 00:24:08.747
- Think of it sooner...
- Oh, my God. We did it!

318
00:24:08.906 --> 00:24:12.160
<i>The link to the lie-detector
test was there the whole time.</i>

319
00:24:12.326 --> 00:24:14.545
<i>It doesn't matter what you say
or what you think.</i>

320
00:24:16.288 --> 00:24:18.666
<i>Your body will always betray you.</i>

321
00:24:21.001 --> 00:24:23.629
Your heart pumps a record of the truth.

322
00:25:15.139 --> 00:25:16.766
So how did the two of you meet?

323
00:25:16.932 --> 00:25:21.062
Well, I'm in SAE,
and Olive is in Alpha O, so...

324
00:25:21.603 --> 00:25:25.824
And all the fellows had
their eyes on her, but I quizzed Mary.

325
00:25:25.983 --> 00:25:27.576
Mary's the AO social chair.

326
00:25:27.735 --> 00:25:29.863
And she told me
that Olive loved begonias...

327
00:25:30.029 --> 00:25:32.532
...so I sent her a bouquet every day...

328
00:25:32.698 --> 00:25:35.542
...till she finally agreed
to take a walk with me.

329
00:25:38.412 --> 00:25:40.255
Smart man.

330
00:25:42.207 --> 00:25:44.756
So Olive tells me you were
a spy in the Great War?

331
00:25:44.918 --> 00:25:47.842
I spent a few years in the OSS.

332
00:25:48.338 --> 00:25:50.466
I shrunk soldiers' heads.

333
00:25:50.632 --> 00:25:53.431
- He's a hero.
- That war was not heroic.

334
00:25:53.594 --> 00:25:56.814
The men I saw,
they experienced unimaginable things.

335
00:25:56.972 --> 00:26:00.021
- I'm sorry. I didn't mean to...
- That's all right.

336
00:26:00.726 --> 00:26:02.774
We're gonna fix it.

337
00:26:02.936 --> 00:26:05.530
Path to peace is not
through finance or politics...

338
00:26:05.689 --> 00:26:07.817
...it is to solve
the problems of man's heart.

339
00:26:07.983 --> 00:26:10.657
Can't solve war
by simply studying men's feelings.

340
00:26:10.819 --> 00:26:12.366
Of course, you're right.

341
00:26:13.363 --> 00:26:15.161
Men's minds are far too limited.

342
00:26:15.949 --> 00:26:17.166
That's why we need women.

343
00:26:19.787 --> 00:26:22.085
Ha-ha. Come on.

344
00:26:22.790 --> 00:26:25.418
We'll see if they'll give us all a ride.

345
00:26:26.460 --> 00:26:28.007
Okay.

346
00:26:28.170 --> 00:26:30.764
- Hey, how are you?
- Good, yourself?

347
00:26:43.060 --> 00:26:45.028
I haven't told Brant...

348
00:26:45.187 --> 00:26:48.782
...but I'm thinking about applying
for the school of journalism at Columbia.

349
00:26:48.941 --> 00:26:50.193
Really?

350
00:26:50.359 --> 00:26:53.533
Oh, well, you'll make
an excellent journalist.

351
00:26:53.695 --> 00:26:56.448
I'll write you a letter
of recommendation, hm?

352
00:26:56.615 --> 00:26:58.367
- Thank you.
- Mm.

353
00:26:58.534 --> 00:27:02.129
Well, Bill and I went to grad school, law.

354
00:27:02.287 --> 00:27:04.585
- Is that where you met?
- Oh, no.

355
00:27:04.748 --> 00:27:06.625
We grew up together.

356
00:27:06.792 --> 00:27:09.170
I've known him my entire life.

357
00:27:09.336 --> 00:27:11.179
I actually came here when...

358
00:27:11.338 --> 00:27:14.512
...I was 5, with my parents
from the Isle of Man.

359
00:27:14.675 --> 00:27:17.849
It's a lovely rock
between England and Ireland.

360
00:27:19.304 --> 00:27:21.398
Were you always sweethearts?

361
00:27:21.557 --> 00:27:24.106
Off and on. Heh.

362
00:27:24.685 --> 00:27:25.902
When were you married?

363
00:27:26.311 --> 00:27:30.157
He came to visit me
at Mount Holyoke, and we... Heh.

364
00:27:30.315 --> 00:27:34.365
We argued forever
about Jung's reaction-time test...

365
00:27:34.528 --> 00:27:36.405
...and then he proposed.

366
00:27:39.241 --> 00:27:40.663
I said no.

367
00:27:40.826 --> 00:27:43.329
- When did you say yes?
- He was very determined.

368
00:27:43.704 --> 00:27:46.799
I said yes eventually,
and then we were married.

369
00:27:48.208 --> 00:27:50.085
Were you in love?

370
00:27:50.252 --> 00:27:52.050
Yes.

371
00:27:52.212 --> 00:27:53.509
Very much.

372
00:27:54.298 --> 00:27:56.471
What made you hesitate?

373
00:28:04.850 --> 00:28:08.070
I was afraid
I would always be in his shadow.

374
00:28:08.228 --> 00:28:10.481
Then why did you say yes?

375
00:28:12.774 --> 00:28:15.118
Because he respects me...

376
00:28:15.986 --> 00:28:18.114
...and he loves me...

377
00:28:19.823 --> 00:28:22.372
...and he's never boring.

378
00:28:24.369 --> 00:28:27.669
I didn't think I'd find those things
in another man.

379
00:28:31.376 --> 00:28:33.674
I see you in everything you do.

380
00:28:37.341 --> 00:28:39.890
I think you're magnificent.

381
00:28:53.232 --> 00:28:54.779
Aren't they beautiful?!

382
00:29:07.788 --> 00:29:09.508
Professor Marston, are you ready?

383
00:29:09.665 --> 00:29:13.169
- Yes, Mrs. Marston, I believe I am.
- Ms. Byrne, are you ready?

384
00:29:13.335 --> 00:29:17.886
- Yes, Mrs. Marston, I believe I am.
- Very well. Right.

385
00:29:18.715 --> 00:29:21.093
Here's to the maiden voyage
of the new...

386
00:29:21.260 --> 00:29:24.139
...and improved lie detector.

387
00:29:24.304 --> 00:29:26.022
Yes.

388
00:29:36.275 --> 00:29:38.198
Is your name...

389
00:29:38.360 --> 00:29:40.283
...William Moulton Marston?

390
00:29:41.530 --> 00:29:42.952
Yes.

391
00:29:44.283 --> 00:29:47.082
True. Where do you live?

392
00:29:48.120 --> 00:29:49.337
Louisiana.

393
00:29:51.665 --> 00:29:53.793
True. False positive.

394
00:29:53.959 --> 00:29:56.178
Who is the president
of the United States?

395
00:29:56.336 --> 00:29:57.929
- Babe Ruth.
- Ha.

396
00:29:59.673 --> 00:30:03.348
True. False positive.

397
00:30:05.095 --> 00:30:07.063
- It doesn't work.
- You've barely started.

398
00:30:07.222 --> 00:30:10.226
Babe Ruth is not the president.
It's not working.

399
00:30:10.392 --> 00:30:12.578
Are you sure you've hooked up
the sphygmomanometer properly?

400
00:30:12.602 --> 00:30:14.980
Of course I hooked up
the sphygmomanometer properly.

401
00:30:15.147 --> 00:30:17.428
Double-check this charge
because this connection is loose.

402
00:30:17.566 --> 00:30:18.783
No, leave it be, you don't...

403
00:30:18.942 --> 00:30:21.115
Perhaps the lies need
to be more meaningful.

404
00:30:23.155 --> 00:30:24.327
What?

405
00:30:24.489 --> 00:30:27.083
Professor Marston
is not invested in whether or not...

406
00:30:27.242 --> 00:30:29.995
...he lives in Boston or Louisiana.

407
00:30:30.495 --> 00:30:33.590
It stands to reason
his blood pressure would not go up.

408
00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:35.880
She's right.

409
00:30:43.759 --> 00:30:45.306
All right.

410
00:30:53.602 --> 00:30:54.774
Do you love your wife?

411
00:30:57.647 --> 00:30:59.240
What?

412
00:31:00.692 --> 00:31:02.660
Do you love your wife?

413
00:31:04.571 --> 00:31:06.039
Yes.

414
00:31:10.952 --> 00:31:12.044
True.

415
00:31:19.628 --> 00:31:21.676
When did you first meet
Ms. Olive Byrne?

416
00:31:21.838 --> 00:31:26.389
She volunteered to work as
a research assistant three months ago.

417
00:31:27.344 --> 00:31:28.391
True.

418
00:31:30.430 --> 00:31:32.979
Are you in love with Olive Byrne?

419
00:31:41.066 --> 00:31:42.113
No.

420
00:31:48.031 --> 00:31:49.157
Hmm.

421
00:31:56.790 --> 00:31:59.384
Well, I guess it works after all.

422
00:32:18.186 --> 00:32:19.233
I don't love him.

423
00:32:20.856 --> 00:32:23.700
- Heh. Of course you do.
- No.

424
00:32:23.859 --> 00:32:25.782
Don't take me for a fool, Olive.

425
00:32:25.944 --> 00:32:27.821
I'm many things, but I'm not a fool.

426
00:32:27.988 --> 00:32:30.867
- I know that. You're brilliant.
- Don't you see? It's over.

427
00:32:31.241 --> 00:32:35.291
- Whatever this is, was, it's over.
- I love you.

428
00:32:43.420 --> 00:32:45.593
Get away from me.

429
00:32:46.256 --> 00:32:48.224
I'm... I'm sorry.

430
00:32:52.512 --> 00:32:56.358
Gather your things.
I want you out of here immediately.

431
00:33:07.027 --> 00:33:08.244
<i>The lie detector...</i>

432
00:33:11.781 --> 00:33:14.330
...it was your wife's idea, wasn't it?

433
00:33:15.869 --> 00:33:18.713
- Well, the systolic-blood-pressure part.
- The important part.

434
00:33:23.168 --> 00:33:25.796
- Elizabeth?
- She's gone.

435
00:33:29.466 --> 00:33:31.764
- I'm sorry if she...
- I don't wanna talk about it.

436
00:33:31.927 --> 00:33:36.023
<i>I met her once years ago.
When she was law clerking.</i>

437
00:33:38.225 --> 00:33:40.353
<i>Makes quite an impression.</i>

438
00:33:42.187 --> 00:33:43.313
Yes, she does.

439
00:33:43.522 --> 00:33:44.944
Hmm.

440
00:33:45.357 --> 00:33:48.952
You've incorporated the lie-detector test
into the <i>Wonder Woman</i> comic...

441
00:33:49.110 --> 00:33:51.784
...her Golden Lasso,
it forces criminals to tell the truth.

442
00:33:52.447 --> 00:33:53.494
That is correct.

443
00:33:53.657 --> 00:33:57.002
Why is Wonder Woman an Amazon?

444
00:33:57.786 --> 00:34:00.915
In Greek mythology, Amazons were
a powerful tribe of women...

445
00:34:01.081 --> 00:34:02.721
- ...who lived without men.
- Without men?

446
00:34:02.749 --> 00:34:04.797
It is important to me that young girls...

447
00:34:04.960 --> 00:34:09.716
...realize they have the power within
themselves to create their own destiny.

448
00:34:10.090 --> 00:34:12.513
To be president
of the United States if they want.

449
00:34:15.011 --> 00:34:19.858
And Wonder Woman's catchphrase
is "Suffering Sappho."

450
00:34:22.143 --> 00:34:25.192
Sappho is a famous poet
from ancient Greece.

451
00:34:25.355 --> 00:34:26.795
<i>Known for her love of women.</i>

452
00:34:26.940 --> 00:34:28.988
<i>It is my belief
that passion and emotion...</i>

453
00:34:29.150 --> 00:34:30.697
<i>...between women is perfectly natural.</i>

454
00:34:30.860 --> 00:34:33.534
<i>Dr. Marston,
lesbianism is an emotional illness.</i>

455
00:34:33.697 --> 00:34:35.074
<i>As a doctor of psychology...</i>

456
00:34:35.240 --> 00:34:37.914
<i>...your endorsement
of this abnormal behavior...</i>

457
00:34:38.076 --> 00:34:41.046
...in the pages of your comic is reckless.

458
00:34:43.540 --> 00:34:45.292
May I take a break, please?

459
00:34:45.458 --> 00:34:47.460
I need to stretch my legs.

460
00:35:02.642 --> 00:35:05.486
- What the fuck are you doing?
- That woman has been an enemy...

461
00:35:05.645 --> 00:35:07.525
...of the Wonder <i>Woman</i> comic
from the beginning.

462
00:35:07.689 --> 00:35:11.284
She's the head of
the Child Study Association of America.

463
00:35:11.443 --> 00:35:15.493
Every parent in America listens
to what she has to say.

464
00:35:15.655 --> 00:35:17.032
I told you to smooth it out.

465
00:35:17.198 --> 00:35:19.792
I mean, we got politicians
sniffing around this thing.

466
00:35:19.951 --> 00:35:21.669
They're talking Senate subcommittees.

467
00:35:21.828 --> 00:35:23.796
You know what that would mean to us?

468
00:35:23.955 --> 00:35:26.049
You got to go in there and play ball.

469
00:35:27.042 --> 00:35:29.465
- And if I don't?
- Then I can't protect you anymore...

470
00:35:29.628 --> 00:35:30.845
...or <i>Wonder Woman.</i>

471
00:35:34.758 --> 00:35:36.556
<i>You've been sad since she left?</i>

472
00:35:37.677 --> 00:35:39.395
I'm not sad.

473
00:35:43.350 --> 00:35:44.397
Hmm.

474
00:35:52.442 --> 00:35:54.536
Maybe I'm in love with her too.

475
00:35:59.199 --> 00:36:01.748
Or maybe I just want her
because you do.

476
00:36:04.079 --> 00:36:07.379
What is it that attracts you to her?

477
00:36:10.210 --> 00:36:12.008
She is beautiful...

478
00:36:13.463 --> 00:36:17.513
...guileless, kind, pure of heart.

479
00:36:19.469 --> 00:36:21.642
And you are brilliant...

480
00:36:21.805 --> 00:36:24.900
...ferocious, hilarious...

481
00:36:25.892 --> 00:36:28.816
...and a grade-A bitch.

482
00:36:33.900 --> 00:36:36.744
Together, you are the perfect woman.

483
00:36:38.738 --> 00:36:40.411
Hmm.

484
00:36:49.207 --> 00:36:53.508
Do you think it's possible
to love two people at the same time?

485
00:37:06.933 --> 00:37:09.607
What we want can never happen.

486
00:37:09.769 --> 00:37:11.567
- Why not?
- Because...

487
00:37:13.398 --> 00:37:16.026
...the world won't let it.

488
00:37:20.155 --> 00:37:22.999
The world can't stop us.

489
00:37:48.767 --> 00:37:52.271
Ms. Byrne, would you mind staying
after class, please?

490
00:37:59.694 --> 00:38:02.823
We've asked you here today
because we are...

491
00:38:02.989 --> 00:38:06.289
Well, we are in something and, uh,
I don't know what it is...

492
00:38:06.451 --> 00:38:07.498
...but we are in it...

493
00:38:07.660 --> 00:38:11.585
...and I feel that I have violated
my raison d'être as a psychologist...

494
00:38:11.748 --> 00:38:15.423
...by running from alarming emotions...

495
00:38:15.585 --> 00:38:17.838
...rather than confronting them,
so here we are.

496
00:38:19.422 --> 00:38:24.269
We were thinking that we could confront
whatever these emotions are together.

497
00:38:25.094 --> 00:38:26.141
Fuck you.

498
00:38:26.304 --> 00:38:28.523
I'm saying,
I'm open to having sex with you...

499
00:38:28.890 --> 00:38:31.769
- ...if you'd like that, as is my husband.
- I'm engaged.

500
00:38:32.268 --> 00:38:34.612
Do you love Brant?

501
00:38:39.400 --> 00:38:42.244
We miss you, Olive.

502
00:38:42.403 --> 00:38:45.452
- We'd like to mend fences.
- Your aunt would approve.

503
00:38:45.824 --> 00:38:48.077
She believed in free love.

504
00:38:52.831 --> 00:38:54.959
Oh, crap. Very well.

505
00:38:55.124 --> 00:39:00.381
If you... If you love this
Brant fellow, then...

506
00:39:00.547 --> 00:39:02.470
Then we're happy for you. Heh.

507
00:39:02.632 --> 00:39:04.760
Let's... Let's forget the sex part.

508
00:39:04.926 --> 00:39:08.897
We can be friends, right?
Let's just all... All be... Be friends.

509
00:39:19.065 --> 00:39:21.193
Yes. Oh, yeah, yeah.

510
00:39:40.086 --> 00:39:44.842
"Olive Byrne is an exceptional student,
a quick study with a passion for learning.

511
00:39:45.008 --> 00:39:47.727
She has a strong work ethic,
a keen mind...

512
00:39:47.886 --> 00:39:49.934
...an unwavering moral compass...

513
00:39:50.722 --> 00:39:53.191
...and a deeply instilled
sense of justice."

514
00:39:56.102 --> 00:39:57.354
There.

515
00:40:00.648 --> 00:40:02.321
Thank you.

516
00:40:02.483 --> 00:40:04.076
Of course.

517
00:40:08.865 --> 00:40:11.914
I'm writing a book. It'll be called
the Emotions <i>of</i> Normal People.

518
00:40:12.076 --> 00:40:14.374
I think you're decidedly not normal.

519
00:40:14.537 --> 00:40:16.960
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Who's to say? Hmm?

520
00:40:17.123 --> 00:40:20.923
We play a sorority game where we guess
what the other person longs for.

521
00:40:21.085 --> 00:40:23.429
- Should we play?
- Sure.

522
00:40:24.672 --> 00:40:27.471
What do I long for?

523
00:40:31.471 --> 00:40:34.771
I think you long
for an unconventional life.

524
00:40:39.395 --> 00:40:40.442
Mm.

525
00:40:47.737 --> 00:40:50.331
How about you, Brant?
What do you think Olive longs for?

526
00:40:54.285 --> 00:40:57.038
I think she longs for your approval.

527
00:41:00.041 --> 00:41:02.794
What is your intention towards Olive?

528
00:41:02.961 --> 00:41:04.759
- I don't understand.
- I didn't ask you.

529
00:41:04.921 --> 00:41:08.095
I know what your intention is,
you're rather obvious.

530
00:41:08.257 --> 00:41:10.885
What is your intention towards Olive?

531
00:41:12.053 --> 00:41:13.805
I don't understand the question.

532
00:41:13.972 --> 00:41:15.474
I'm not an idiot.

533
00:41:15.640 --> 00:41:17.893
You're filling her mind
with perverse ideas.

534
00:41:18.059 --> 00:41:21.529
Olive is a good person with a pure heart
and you are trying to corrupt her.

535
00:41:21.688 --> 00:41:23.816
You cannot corrupt somebody with ideas.

536
00:41:23.982 --> 00:41:27.156
- It is ignorance that is corrupting.
- Do not lecture me, professor.

537
00:41:27.318 --> 00:41:30.367
- I am not one of your students.
- Bill, Brant, this is unnecessary.

538
00:41:30.530 --> 00:41:34.125
I am trying to see what you see in them,
but I'm sorry, I do not.

539
00:41:34.283 --> 00:41:36.285
- They're my friends.
- They're reprobate.

540
00:41:38.079 --> 00:41:39.296
Don't you see that?

541
00:41:39.455 --> 00:41:42.425
Look, Olive is not a child,
you can't control her.

542
00:41:42.583 --> 00:41:45.757
You can't stick a ring on her finger
and put her in a box for your mantel...

543
00:41:45.920 --> 00:41:47.680
...a good little woman
behind her little man.

544
00:41:47.839 --> 00:41:49.307
- I love her.
- Oh...

545
00:41:49.465 --> 00:41:51.559
And I will fight for her.

546
00:41:52.218 --> 00:41:54.516
Brant, please?

547
00:41:56.431 --> 00:41:59.105
Olive and I are to be married,
so as her future husband...

548
00:41:59.267 --> 00:42:02.237
...I would appreciate it
if you would confine your relationship...

549
00:42:02.812 --> 00:42:05.486
- ...to the classroom.
- Is this what you want?

550
00:42:08.192 --> 00:42:10.035
- Let's go.
- I'm sorry.

551
00:43:06.459 --> 00:43:07.927
What are you doing here?

552
00:43:10.004 --> 00:43:11.677
I don't know.

553
00:43:18.971 --> 00:43:20.598
What is your name?

554
00:43:20.932 --> 00:43:22.730
Olive Byrne.

555
00:43:23.267 --> 00:43:24.940
That is correct. How old are you?

556
00:43:25.103 --> 00:43:26.605
Twenty-two.

557
00:43:29.023 --> 00:43:30.696
That is true.

558
00:43:32.068 --> 00:43:33.115
Why are you here?

559
00:43:34.821 --> 00:43:36.539
I don't know.

560
00:43:36.697 --> 00:43:38.324
That is true.

561
00:43:38.491 --> 00:43:40.289
What do you want?

562
00:43:43.412 --> 00:43:45.085
I don't know.

563
00:43:48.584 --> 00:43:49.961
That is a lie.

564
00:43:53.506 --> 00:43:55.099
