00:50:31.654 --> 00:50:34.032
<i>♪ For me ♪</i>

610
00:50:51.465 --> 00:50:57.143
<i>♪ I'm feelin' good ♪</i>

611
00:51:18.242 --> 00:51:19.835
Love leaders.

612
00:51:19.994 --> 00:51:23.669
<i>If the nature of men is
inherently violent and anarchistic...</i>

613
00:51:25.416 --> 00:51:29.011
...and the nature of women
is inherently loving and nurturing...

614
00:51:30.963 --> 00:51:33.933
...then shouldn't women be
the ones to rule the world?

615
00:51:35.801 --> 00:51:37.803
Wouldn't that be
a more reasonable choice?

616
00:51:44.727 --> 00:51:45.819
But be warned, ladies.

617
00:51:45.978 --> 00:51:48.777
We men will not give up
our power without a fight.

618
00:51:57.156 --> 00:51:59.875
I wasn't expecting you until later.

619
00:52:02.036 --> 00:52:03.754
Are you all right?

620
00:52:05.539 --> 00:52:07.758
Everybody knows, Olive.

621
00:52:10.628 --> 00:52:13.598
You haven't even bothered
being discreet.

622
00:52:17.343 --> 00:52:18.720
- I don't know what...
- Please.

623
00:52:20.179 --> 00:52:23.729
I could ask you
to stop seeing them again...

624
00:52:25.809 --> 00:52:27.561
...but I know that you will not.

625
00:53:07.976 --> 00:53:09.774
We've been fired.

626
00:53:16.402 --> 00:53:19.155
I want to be with you.
I want to be with both of you.

627
00:53:19.321 --> 00:53:22.074
- Yes. Yes.
- Are you both insane?

628
00:53:22.700 --> 00:53:26.955
Do you not realize what has happened?
We are ruined. All of us.

629
00:53:27.121 --> 00:53:28.498
You will not be able to marry.

630
00:53:28.664 --> 00:53:31.668
You will not be able to teach.
I will not be able to do anything.

631
00:53:31.834 --> 00:53:33.802
What kind of a world
do you think we're living in?

632
00:53:33.961 --> 00:53:37.886
- We are in love.
- We cannot be in love.

633
00:53:38.048 --> 00:53:40.801
- It's unorthodox, sure, but it's...
- It's preposterous.

634
00:53:40.968 --> 00:53:45.474
It is a fantasy,
and we have to live in reality.

635
00:53:45.639 --> 00:53:50.236
And in this world
and these lives, love...

636
00:53:50.394 --> 00:53:53.273
- ...it doesn't matter.
- I don't believe that.

637
00:53:54.148 --> 00:53:56.401
Well, then you're a fool.

638
00:53:56.567 --> 00:54:00.413
A stupid, simpering dilettante.

639
00:54:04.158 --> 00:54:05.250
I'm pregnant.

640
00:54:08.996 --> 00:54:10.043
<i>Dr. Marston?</i>

641
00:54:14.793 --> 00:54:16.873
- Sorry. What?
- You were saying that Wonder Woman...

642
00:54:16.962 --> 00:54:19.385
...leaves Paradise Island
and enters man's world.

643
00:54:19.548 --> 00:54:21.676
That's what you call it, right?
Man's world.

644
00:54:22.342 --> 00:54:23.514
Yes.

645
00:54:27.973 --> 00:54:30.692
We don't even have enough money
to pay for the electricity.

646
00:54:30.851 --> 00:54:32.912
We still have some money coming in
from my book sales.

647
00:54:32.936 --> 00:54:35.439
Oh, all five of them?

648
00:54:36.023 --> 00:54:40.779
I'm sorry, dear, but nobody gives a shit
about DISC theory.

649
00:54:42.863 --> 00:54:45.787
What about you? You're here now.
You can pull your weight.

650
00:54:45.949 --> 00:54:48.077
- She's pregnant.
- Obviously.

651
00:54:48.243 --> 00:54:51.167
- You said it was all right if I stayed.
- As if I had a choice.

652
00:54:51.330 --> 00:54:52.798
- Then I'll go.
- No.

653
00:54:52.956 --> 00:54:55.459
What about your famous feminist aunt?
She's rich.

654
00:54:57.753 --> 00:55:01.348
She's worried that any association
with our situation...

655
00:55:01.507 --> 00:55:03.885
...would be bad for the movement.

656
00:55:04.051 --> 00:55:05.724
What a bitch.

657
00:55:07.930 --> 00:55:10.058
I read in the paper
the Keelers are making money...

658
00:55:10.224 --> 00:55:11.942
...selling the lie-detector machine.

659
00:55:12.100 --> 00:55:13.818
Perhaps we could do the same.

660
00:55:13.977 --> 00:55:17.231
That's an excellent idea, Olive.
Perhaps Bill should have patented it.

661
00:55:17.397 --> 00:55:20.742
Science is for everybody,
for the greater good.

662
00:55:20.901 --> 00:55:21.993
I was right to publish.

663
00:55:22.152 --> 00:55:24.088
The greater good won't feed your child.

664
00:55:24.112 --> 00:55:25.455
It's your child also.

665
00:55:25.614 --> 00:55:28.163
- You'd be responsible too if you...
- What? Had a click?

666
00:55:28.325 --> 00:55:30.293
You know what I mean.

667
00:55:48.595 --> 00:55:50.142
Olive.

668
00:56:30.137 --> 00:56:32.640
- How many words a minute do you type?
- Seventy-five.

669
00:56:32.806 --> 00:56:35.104
- Can you take dictation?
- Well, I can learn.

670
00:56:35.267 --> 00:56:37.770
It's just that there are
spurious rumors out there...

671
00:56:37.936 --> 00:56:40.064
...maligning my reputation.

672
00:56:40.230 --> 00:56:44.781
There has been talk of some
improprieties while you were at Radcliffe.

673
00:56:44.943 --> 00:56:46.911
You have a degree in law
from Boston University...

674
00:56:47.070 --> 00:56:49.448
...and a master's degree
in psychology from Radcliffe.

675
00:56:49.615 --> 00:56:51.242
Harvard.

676
00:56:51.950 --> 00:56:56.296
- And are you all still together?
- That won't get in the way, will it?

677
00:56:56.455 --> 00:56:58.958
I don't see how my personal life
is anyone's business.

678
00:56:59.124 --> 00:57:01.547
It's time to move on, Bill.

679
00:57:01.919 --> 00:57:04.513
You don't think you're too good
for this line of work?

680
00:57:06.465 --> 00:57:07.887
No.

681
00:57:39.706 --> 00:57:41.754
I want him to grow up with a family.

682
00:57:46.088 --> 00:57:47.715
I want more for him.

683
00:57:48.757 --> 00:57:50.930
More than I had.

684
00:57:58.475 --> 00:57:59.943
If...

685
00:58:01.144 --> 00:58:04.523
If we do this, we can't let it
come back on our children.

686
00:58:04.690 --> 00:58:07.944
We'll have to make up an explanation...

687
00:58:08.694 --> 00:58:10.492
...a lie...

688
00:58:12.864 --> 00:58:14.912
...and stick to it.

689
00:58:32.884 --> 00:58:35.012
<i>Wonder Woman has a secret identity.</i>

690
00:58:35.178 --> 00:58:36.680
- Yes, she does.
- Why is that?

691
00:58:36.847 --> 00:58:40.317
She has to hide her true self
from man's world.

692
00:58:41.143 --> 00:58:43.612
Hi, I'm Molly Stewart
from across the street.

693
00:58:43.770 --> 00:58:46.273
- I wanted to come over and say hello.
- Hello.

694
00:58:46.440 --> 00:58:48.192
It was silly
that you've been living here...

695
00:58:48.358 --> 00:58:51.453
...for over a week and we haven't
been properly introduced.

696
00:58:51.611 --> 00:58:52.783
Are you Mrs. Marston?

697
00:58:52.946 --> 00:58:54.698
No, I'm Mrs. Marston, hello.

698
00:58:54.865 --> 00:58:57.539
Hello. And you?

699
00:58:57.701 --> 00:58:59.920
Oh, I just live here.

700
00:59:00.829 --> 00:59:03.127
Oh. So Byrne is your son?

701
00:59:03.290 --> 00:59:05.338
He wandered over yesterday,
wanting to play.

702
00:59:05.500 --> 00:59:08.128
No, no, Byrne's my son.
I have two sons, Donn and Byrne.

703
00:59:09.546 --> 00:59:12.641
My husband Richard passed away,
so the Marstons took us in.

704
00:59:12.799 --> 00:59:14.016
You poor dear.

705
00:59:14.176 --> 00:59:15.678
Pete is my boy.

706
00:59:16.178 --> 00:59:19.728
Well, it's been good to meet you.
I'm sure we'll see you again.

707
00:59:19.890 --> 00:59:22.234
- See you soon.
- Nice to meet you both.

708
00:59:22.768 --> 00:59:24.816
Donn, Byrne, Peter.

709
00:59:24.978 --> 00:59:26.571
Come on, boys.

710
00:59:26.730 --> 00:59:29.153
<i>Dear Aunt Margaret,
things are good here...</i>

711
00:59:29.316 --> 00:59:31.489
<i>...and we're settling in to our new rental.</i>

712
00:59:31.651 --> 00:59:34.655
<i>The kids are keeping me busy,
and we're very happy here.</i>

713
00:59:34.821 --> 00:59:37.119
<i>I'm submitting writing samples
to publishers...</i>

714
00:59:37.282 --> 00:59:39.000
<i>...and hope someone bites soon.</i>

715
00:59:39.159 --> 00:59:40.786
Would you say she was living a lie?

716
00:59:40.952 --> 00:59:43.125
No, Wonder Woman assumes
an alter ego...

717
00:59:43.288 --> 00:59:46.383
...so she can go to work
as Steve Trevor's secretary.

718
00:59:46.541 --> 00:59:48.009
<i>She's a secretary?</i>

719
00:59:48.168 --> 00:59:49.968
<i>What's wrong
with being a secretary?</i>

720
00:59:50.045 --> 00:59:52.548
Nothing's wrong with that,
but I think it's odd...

721
00:59:52.714 --> 00:59:56.389
...that Wonder Woman is all-powerful
and you have her hiding as a secretary.

722
00:59:57.219 --> 00:59:58.436
She's a modern woman.

723
00:59:58.887 --> 01:00:00.981
- Hello.
- Hello.

724
01:00:01.139 --> 01:00:03.767
Hi, you look lovely.

725
01:00:03.934 --> 01:00:05.811
- Oh, so do you.
- Hello, boys.

726
01:00:05.977 --> 01:00:08.856
<i>She has a career of
her own, she makes her own money.</i>

727
01:00:09.022 --> 01:00:11.320
- Where's Bill?
- In his office.

728
01:00:11.817 --> 01:00:14.741
<i>She is not dependent on a man.</i>

729
01:00:21.493 --> 01:00:23.871
"You too can be popular."

730
01:00:24.037 --> 01:00:26.586
This one's going to sell. I'm sure of it.

731
01:00:31.878 --> 01:00:33.880
<i>So then why the elaborate charade?</i>

732
01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:45.475
This... This... This is for you.

